    {
      "title": "Write Short Notes",
      "type": "qa",
      "items": [
        {
          "question": "Define a map.",
          "answer": "A map is a drawing of the Earth, countries, states and even cities on a flat surface.",
          "sources": {
            "textbook": true
          }
        },
        {
          "question": "What are oceans? Name the five oceans.",
          "answer": [
            "The very large water bodies are called oceans. There are five oceans:",
            "Pacific Ocean",
            "Atlantic Ocean",
            "Indian Ocean",
            "Arctic Ocean",
            "Antarctic Ocean"
          ],
          "sources": {
            "notes": true
          }
        },
        {
          "question": "What are continents? Name the seven continents.",
          "answer": [
            "Large land masses are called continents. The seven continents are:",
            "Asia",
            "Europe",
            "Africa",
            "Australia",
            "Antarctica",
            "North America",
            "South America"
          ],
          "sources": {
            "notes": true
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Answer the Following Questions",
      "type": "qa",
      "items": [
        {
          "question": "Name the four directions with the help of a labelled diagram.",
          "answer": [
            "There are four main directions: north, south, east and west.",
            "The Sun rises in the east and sets in the west. When you stand facing the rising Sun, east is in front and west behind you. North is on your left and south on your right.",
            "North is at the top, South at the bottom, East on the right and West on the left."
          ],
          "sources": {
            "notes": true
          }
        },
        {
          "question": "Why is a map more convenient than a globe?",
          "answer": "A map can be folded and carried easily. Besides, a large wall map can be hung on the wall so that everybody can see the details clearly.",
          "sources": {
            "notes": true
          }
        },
        {
          "question": "What is the difference between a wall map and an atlas?",
          "answer": "Wall maps are big and can be hung on the wall in the classroom so that all children can see the details, whereas an atlas is a book of maps and it is easy to carry.",
          "sources": {
            "notes": true
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Application Based Questions",
      "type": "qa",
      "items": [
        {
          "question": "You want to find the shortest route from your house to the nearest railway station. Would you use a map or a globe? Give a reason for your answer.",
          "answer": "I would use a map to find the shortest route from my house to the nearest railway station, because a map shows details of a place clearly.",
          "sources": {
            "notes": true
          }
        }
      ]
    },
