    {
      "title": "Points to Remember",
      "type": "block",
      "items": [
        {
          "heading": "Points to Remember",
          "lines": [
            "A globe is a model of the Earth.",
            "A map is a drawing of the Earth.",
            "An atlas is a book of maps.",
            "Very large water bodies are called oceans.",
            "North, south, east and west are the four main directions.",
            "A globe shows only one part of the Earth at a time, so it has to be rotated. It cannot show all the details.",
            "There are five oceans: Pacific, Atlantic, Indian, Arctic and Antarctic. The Pacific is the largest and deepest; the Arctic is the smallest.",
            "There are seven continents: Asia, Africa, North America, South America, Europe, Australia and Antarctica.",
            "A compass needle always points towards the north."
          ],
          "sources": {
            "textbook": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "layout": "list"
